Default CVS to the IPU bridge when media ancillary autoselection is enabled.

The CVS prompt is inside the hidden miscellaneous-helper menu when
MEDIA_SUBDRV_AUTOSELECT=y, but no parent driver selects it. Consequently
olddefconfig discards an explicit CONFIG_VIDEO_INTEL_CVS=m.

Keep the helper-menu placement chosen in the upstream v2 series:
https://lore.kernel.org/linux-media/20260514184431.288353-1-miguel.vadillo@intel.com/
A conditional default preserves that placement and honours the existing
I2C, ACPI, VIDEO_DEV and optional IPU_BRIDGE dependency bounds. Manual
configuration remains available with ancillary autoselection disabled.
This is a proposed integration correction, not an accepted upstream patch.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/cvs/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/cvs/Kconfig
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@ config VIDEO_INTEL_CVS
 	select MEDIA_CONTROLLER
 	select VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API
 	select V4L2_FWNODE
+	default IPU_BRIDGE if MEDIA_SUBDRV_AUTOSELECT
 	help
 	  This adds support for the Intel Computer Vision Sensing (CVS).
 
